WEBVTT

0
00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:00.769
First,

1
00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:02.450
let's cover the basics.

2
00:00:02.769 --> 00:00:06.010
Let's discuss key aspects of Stanford's compensation philosophy.

3
00:00:06.289 --> 00:00:08.029
What is a compensation philosophy?

4
00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:09.159
At its core,

5
00:00:09.409 --> 00:00:12.670
a compensation philosophy is a formal guiding statement

6
00:00:12.670 --> 00:00:15.550
by executive leadership that defines an organization's,

7
00:00:15.890 --> 00:00:16.450
in this case,

8
00:00:16.610 --> 00:00:17.659
Stanford's commitment.

9
00:00:17.979 --> 00:00:19.889
And strategy to market positioning,

10
00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:21.969
equity and performance.

11
00:00:22.219 --> 00:00:23.780
Our compensation philosophy

12
00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:25.649
is aligned with Stanford's values,

13
00:00:25.899 --> 00:00:28.920
goals and objectives with respect to its workforce

14
00:00:29.139 --> 00:00:30.040
or human capital.

15
00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:31.209
As a manager,

16
00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:33.979
it is important that you understand key aspects

17
00:00:33.979 --> 00:00:37.759
of Stanford's compensation philosophy and apply its principles

18
00:00:37.979 --> 00:00:39.459
with guidance from your HR partner.

19
00:00:39.990 --> 00:00:43.220
To support consistent and equitable compensation decisions.

20
00:00:43.590 --> 00:00:44.979
Let's now take a look at a

21
00:00:44.979 --> 00:00:48.009
few important aspects of Stanford's compensation philosophy.

22
00:00:48.229 --> 00:00:49.139
At Stanford,

23
00:00:49.389 --> 00:00:53.569
we are committed to providing a fair and competitive staff compensation program

24
00:00:53.709 --> 00:00:54.509
that will attract,

25
00:00:54.659 --> 00:00:55.330
retain

26
00:00:55.430 --> 00:00:56.209
and reward

27
00:00:56.349 --> 00:00:58.419
high performing employees at all levels.

28
00:00:58.549 --> 00:01:01.009
This is foundational to our compensation philosophy.

29
00:01:01.759 --> 00:01:05.839
While there are 7 core guiding principles of Stanford's compensation philosophy,

30
00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:09.839
we will focus today on the 3 objectives most relevant to managers.

31
00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:10.839
These are

32
00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:13.160
external market competitiveness,

33
00:01:13.459 --> 00:01:14.860
internal comparability,

34
00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:17.080
And performance recognition.

35
00:01:17.889 --> 00:01:20.190
We'll detail each of these momentarily.

36
00:01:20.410 --> 00:01:21.250
As a manager,

37
00:01:21.449 --> 00:01:22.529
your focus when it comes to

38
00:01:22.529 --> 00:01:25.529
these three aspects of Stanford's compensation philosophy

39
00:01:25.730 --> 00:01:27.669
should be consulting with your HR partner

40
00:01:27.809 --> 00:01:29.669
to balance these core objectives together

41
00:01:29.970 --> 00:01:31.800
when making compensation decisions.

42
00:01:31.930 --> 00:01:35.930
This is important because this balance enables Stanford to successfully recruit,

43
00:01:36.290 --> 00:01:36.949
recognize

44
00:01:37.169 --> 00:01:38.400
and retain our talent

45
00:01:38.660 --> 00:01:42.309
while upholding our commitment to fiscal affordability for the university.

46
00:01:42.529 --> 00:01:43.319
Remember,

47
00:01:43.769 --> 00:01:47.190
you do not need to be a compensation expert in order to support this balance.

48
00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:50.540
Do your best to understand the basics and work with your

49
00:01:50.540 --> 00:01:53.160
HR partners to find the right balance for your team.

50
00:01:53.459 --> 00:01:53.980
Now,

51
00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:57.930
let's take a moment to dig into the details of each of these core objectives.

52
00:01:58.019 --> 00:02:00.080
The first core principle to keep in mind

53
00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:02.120
is external market competitiveness.

54
00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:03.220
At Stanford,

55
00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:05.360
external market competitiveness

56
00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:06.599
means that we reflect

57
00:02:07.050 --> 00:02:10.000
market competitive pay rates for comparable jobs

58
00:02:10.220 --> 00:02:11.160
based on

59
00:02:11.419 --> 00:02:14.580
the market benchmarks in the location where work is performed.

60
00:02:14.979 --> 00:02:16.199
Role requirements,

61
00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:18.529
which reflect the roles scope and complexity,

62
00:02:19.059 --> 00:02:21.580
education and relevant experience for the role and demand

63
00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:23.580
for such roles within the relevant labor market.

64
00:02:23.660 --> 00:02:26.100
The target market position for each individual job may

65
00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:28.960
vary based on what is competitive for the position.

66
00:02:29.539 --> 00:02:32.139
Consult with your local HR partner to better understand

67
00:02:32.139 --> 00:02:34.479
what the competitive range is for each position.

68
00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:36.559
The next core principle to keep in mind

69
00:02:36.699 --> 00:02:38.199
is internal comparability.

70
00:02:38.559 --> 00:02:41.059
This means that Stanford provides pay guidelines

71
00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:44.740
that ensure similar jobs are paid equitably across the university.

72
00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:45.789
As a manager,

73
00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:48.309
these pay guidelines are important to understand,

74
00:02:48.679 --> 00:02:51.190
especially when it comes to justifiable pay differences.

75
00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:54.699
It's important to remember that pay equity does not necessarily mean

76
00:02:54.699 --> 00:02:57.720
that all employees in the same job receive the same pay.

77
00:02:58.380 --> 00:03:01.080
There are reasons pay may be different and still equitable.

78
00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:03.500
Pay differences may reflect variations in

79
00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:06.139
compensable factors such as experience,

80
00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:07.970
subject matter expertise,

81
00:03:08.419 --> 00:03:09.050
performance,

82
00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:10.309
work location,

83
00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:12.360
and other acceptable reasons

84
00:03:12.740 --> 00:03:14.089
without regard to gender,

85
00:03:14.380 --> 00:03:14.960
race,

86
00:03:15.139 --> 00:03:15.779
age,

87
00:03:16.139 --> 00:03:17.059
disability,

88
00:03:17.419 --> 00:03:18.699
sexual orientation.

89
00:03:18.990 --> 00:03:21.250
Or other legally protected categories.

90
00:03:21.509 --> 00:03:24.089
The 3rd core principle that managers should understand

91
00:03:24.190 --> 00:03:25.669
is performance recognition.

92
00:03:25.860 --> 00:03:26.699
At Stanford,

93
00:03:26.869 --> 00:03:29.570
we acknowledge outstanding performance through rewards

94
00:03:29.679 --> 00:03:32.929
that highlight significant contributions to the organization

95
00:03:33.110 --> 00:03:34.270
and support retention.

96
00:03:34.509 --> 00:03:37.850
Recognition could take the form of salary increases and

97
00:03:38.070 --> 00:03:41.690
or other one-time compensation rewards as appropriate.

98
00:03:41.830 --> 00:03:44.729
Through your role in performance management and salary planning.

99
00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:47.220
As appropriate to your school or unit,

100
00:03:47.539 --> 00:03:51.160
recognition is one of the primary ways that you as a manager,

101
00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:54.360
support the delivery of Stanford's compensation philosophy.

102
00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:57.679
In addition to the core pillars of external market competitiveness,

103
00:03:58.179 --> 00:03:59.559
internal comparability

104
00:03:59.740 --> 00:04:01.169
and performance recognition,

105
00:04:01.490 --> 00:04:04.600
transparency is an important concept for managers to keep in mind.

106
00:04:04.979 --> 00:04:08.500
It is also the 4th pillar of Stanford's compensation philosophy.

107
00:04:09.339 --> 00:04:10.179
At Stanford,

108
00:04:10.440 --> 00:04:14.149
pay transparency is focused on effectively communicating pay decisions

109
00:04:14.149 --> 00:04:16.209
to staff in a clear and informed way.

110
00:04:16.390 --> 00:04:20.899
We also enable pay transparency by making Stanford's compensation policies,

111
00:04:21.149 --> 00:04:24.700
procedures and assistance services available and accessible.

112
00:04:24.899 --> 00:04:27.869
Stanford also supports pay transparency by including

113
00:04:27.869 --> 00:04:29.890
a pay range on every job posting.

114
00:04:30.380 --> 00:04:32.940
Employees are also entitled to request and receive

115
00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:34.769
the pay range for their current position.

116
00:04:35.019 --> 00:04:39.459
Please remember that individual compensation information is sensitive

117
00:04:39.459 --> 00:04:41.730
information that needs to be managed appropriately.

118
00:04:41.980 --> 00:04:45.279
While you can discuss an employee's pay and pay range with them,

119
00:04:45.739 --> 00:04:47.529
you should never share or discuss

120
00:04:47.529 --> 00:04:50.179
the compensation information of another employee.
